# =============================================================================
# 11. BRIER-DERIVED RELIABILITY
# =============================================================================

RELIABILITY_DEFINITION = r"""
R_T = 1 - Brier_T

The resulting R_T is referred to as the Brier-derived reliability
component throughout the framework. It provides a bounded, higher-is-better
summary of probabilistic prediction quality, while the original Brier score
is retained for direct reporting.

This quantity is not treated as a complete calibration analysis.
ECE, reliability diagrams, and NLL remain complementary diagnostics.
"""


# =============================================================================
# 12. CROSS-DOMAIN PERFORMANCE CONSISTENCY
# =============================================================================

CROSS_DOMAIN_CONSISTENCY = r"""
C_ST = (2 * F_S * F_T) / (F_S + F_T)

where:

    F_S = source-validation Macro-F1
    F_T = target-test Macro-F1

C_ST is used as a complementary source-to-target consistency diagnostic.
It is not included in the CDRI3 composite score.
"""


# =============================================================================
# 13. CROSS-DOMAIN ROBUSTNESS INDEX
# =============================================================================

CDRI3_DEFINITION = r"""
CDRI3 = [F_1,T + H_T + (1 - Brier_T)] / 3

where:

    F_1,T       = target-domain Macro-F1
    H_T         = target-domain harmful-class recall
    Brier_T     = target-domain Brier score

CDRI3 is a measurement component within CDRF. It is not a replacement
for the broader CDRF evaluation protocol.

Equal weighting is used as the transparent reference configuration.
Weight sensitivity is subsequently evaluated rather than assuming that
equal weighting is universally optimal.
"""


