        Apply the documented dataset eligibility and label-processing rules.

    STEP 3
        Reconstruct or use the frozen split manifests supplied with the
        repository.

    STEP 4
        Generate the frozen CLIP ViT-B/32 image and text representations.

    STEP 5
        Construct the 1024-dimensional multimodal representation.

    STEP 6
        Train the three downstream strategies using the documented
        configurations:
            Logistic Regression
            MLP
            XGBoost

    STEP 7
        Execute the S1 source-only protocol.

    STEP 8
        Execute the S2 source + target-adaptation protocol.

    STEP 9
        Select target-domain thresholds using target validation Macro-F1,
        applying the documented tie-breaking rule.

    STEP 10
        Evaluate once on the strictly held-out target test set.

    STEP 11
        Calculate Accuracy, Macro-F1, Harmful Recall, Brier Score,
        Brier-derived Reliability and NLL.

    STEP 12
        Calculate C_ST and CDRI3.

    STEP 13
        Repeat the required analysis across seeds 42--46.

    STEP 14
        Perform bootstrap uncertainty analysis, leave-one-component-out
        analysis, weight sensitivity, reverse transfer, and external
        MultiOFF validation.

    STEP 15
        Compare model rankings produced by CDRI3 and the individual metrics.

The frozen manifests and configuration artifacts should be treated as the
authoritative source for exact split reconstruction and protocol details.
"""


